cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "passmcp-graph: a local graph of agents, MCP servers, tools and identities"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rousseau
    given-names: Sebastien
    email: sebastian.rousseau@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/sebastienrousseau/passmcp-graph"
url: "https://sebastienrousseau.com/passmcp-graph/"
abstract: >-
  A command-line tool that builds a local graph of which agents use which
  Model Context Protocol servers, which tools those servers expose and which
  identities reach them, from passmcp's attestations and reports and from MCP
  client configurations. It names inherited critical findings and
  over-privileged identities, answers path queries offline, gates on
  forbidden-path policies in CI, and exports JSON, GraphML and Cypher. It
  makes no network request and stores no credential.
keywords:
  - model-context-protocol
  - mcp
  - graph
  - policy
  - attestation
  - golang
license: GPL-3.0-only
version: 0.0.1
date-released: "2026-09-29"
